 "text": "Hi, how are you doing right now? Okay, sounds good. Living with a host family gives you real-life experience, which is great. The school in Valencia gives you real talking time with natives. Volunteering is great for practical skills, but language use depends on the place. I'd lean towards the school in Valencia, if you can afford it. Twenty hours a week is good pace, and the shared flat means you don't have to cook or clean. Volunteering is good too, but it relies on the place. Living with a host family is nice, but it depends on how host the family is.",
